tain, Germany, and Canada places Mr Lee firmly inside a Western-co-convened security coalition, a register that sits in some tension with his January visit to Beijing.\n\nThe week's economic signals were equally expansive. At parliamentary confirmation hearings on April 15, incoming Bank of Korea governor Shin Hyun-song reversed his prior neutral stance on the won, warned against \"sharp weakening,",
